                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I like the idea and execution of Technosphere but there is no reason to purchase it at this point.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/WOjM1hS1tPE?t=2h6m56s\n\nTechnosphere is a puzzle platformer where you control a sphere and roll it around two different levels. You can use switches, have your jump ability turned off and utilize physics controls to move yourself across the level.\n\nThe best asset in Technosphere is the lighting. The game has some really cool lighting effects that are a joy to watch in action. I really want this to be refined further as more levels are released.\n\nThe actual game and levels are where the game falls short currently. There are only two levels available in this version of the Early Access release. They seem to loop as well instead of having a pure end point.\n\nBecause of the lack of content I cannot currently recommend Technosphere, even as an early access product. The current build is better suited for a website like itch.io as a tech demo rather than any sort of release on Steam, Early Access or otherwise.\n\nAs a note to the developer, I see potential in this game and if you update it to be more like a proper game release, please let me know so I can check it out again and update my review.\n\nIf you found this review helpful, follow my Curator page to see everything I cover. http://store.steampowered.com/curator/29029552/",
